---
/**
 * Starlight's theme provider, pinned to dark (GP-213).
 *
 * Upstream this reads `localStorage` and `prefers-color-scheme` and writes the
 * result to `data-theme`. This site has one theme — carbon, the identity the
 * product ships in — so it writes `dark` unconditionally.
 *
 * This is not cosmetic. Starlight's own components key off `data-theme`, and so
 * does Expressive Code, which emits **two** colours per syntax token and picks
 * between them with a `[data-theme='light']` rule. Left to the visitor's OS,
 * somebody in light mode read light-theme tokens on our permanently dark code
 * blocks. Pinning the attribute makes every one of those rules agree with the
 * palette instead of fighting it.
 *
 * The script is inline and runs before paint, so there is no flash — and the
 * attribute is also set on the server-rendered `<html>` element, so a visitor
 * with JavaScript off gets the same page.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "dark";
</script>
